h, we see that the range of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\n0 \\leq f(x) \\lt 9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f^{-1}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n0 \\leq x \\lt 9.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179423 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10810" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179423 #edb/ref 1071 "The domain of the function $f(x)$ is $-3\\lt x \\leq 3$ and the range of $f$ is $-2\\leq f(x) \\lt 2.$ What is the range of the inverse function $f^{-1}(x)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179423 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3d784815-6930-5b44-b1a4-6cf2d3e2eeb0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179423 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we recall the following:\n\n- The domain of a function $f(x)$ is the range of its inverse function $f^{-1}(x).$\n\n- The range of a function $f(x)$ is the domain of its inverse function $f^{-1}(x).$\n\nThe domain of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\n-3\\lt x \\leq 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f^{-1}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n-3\\lt  f^{-1}(x) \\leq 3.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179424 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10823" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179424 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/c1/c187a2fdc4c34135836afd2f28af17776cee6408b1e7bf3124d4833ca0529000.png)\n\nFor the function $y = f(x)$ shown above, what is the range of the inverse function $f^{-1}(x)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179424 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "93801dca-c5a6-5c7e-b10b-1e407332927a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179424 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we recall the following:\n\n- The domain of a function $f(x)$ is the range of its inverse function $f^{-1}(x).$\n\n- The range of a function $f(x)$ is the domain of its inverse function $f^{-1}(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the domain of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\n-1 \\lt x \\lt 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f^{-1}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n-1 \\lt f^{-1}(x) \\lt 4.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179755 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179755 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179755 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180081 #edb/ref 1